INV-kazij's test fails ONLY in the full-suite CI container — never
locally on any tree, in any interleaving (single test / whole core
suite / cross-package under xdist), with or without the meta-package.
The owner-fired parity cron (dev 8e913045e0, meta installed, wheel
built, 9 previously-skipped tests un-skipped) failed identically, which
eliminates the install-set hypothesis — the last cheap one.

So the assertion becomes the instrument: on failure it now reports
(a) the toml-config pass's run rows (did the analyzer run, how many
files/nodes), (b) every node on the pyproject path with kind + meta
(was the script symbol emitted, with which concepts), and (c) the
derived entrypoint kinds. The three candidate break points — analyzer
skipped, concept not emitted, conversion dropped — produce three
different messages, so the next red cron is a mechanism reading
instead of a fourth repetition of 'assert []'.

